Apple's new iPad specific OS or iPad OS  is coming this fall and it's bringing a  bunch of new features that make it more  like a computer than ever before  in this video is a full guide on how to  use the new split view in multitasking  features so let's get started  multitasking starts with the app dock so  let's fill it up with the apps we'll use  every day something new this year is the  ability to put entire app folders onto  the dock so you can have access to any  app you want from just the dock  starting with slide over mode first open  an app then swipe up from the bottom to  bring up the dock then drag an app onto  the side of the screen but don't drag it  to the very edge you can now use both  apps at the same time or drag items from  one app into the other like images links  or files you can also swipe the bar on  the bottom of the slide over window to  switch between other apps you have open  and slide over mode or you can swipe up  on that bar to show all of the apps at  once and choose which one you'd like to  use you can also drag the top of the  slide over a window to the other side of  the screen  slide over mode is very useful for doing  things like quickly bringing up the  files app and dragging files into apps  like luma fusion for video editing if  you don't have the desired app open in  one of your slide over windows just drag  the app from the dock and it'll replace  the current app once you're finished  just grab the edge of the window and  swipe it off the screen and you can  swipe again to bring it back to switch  the split view mode just pull the top  bar down and into the edge of the screen  at that point you can bring back the  slide over window by swiping from the  edge you can move it to the other side  just as before and pulling down on the  slide over apps top bar will replace the  underlying split view app you can easily  swap the positions of the apps by  dragging the top bar of an app to the  other side you can also drag the bar in  the center of the apps to give more  space to either app either in a 50/50 or  25/75 split to replace an app while and  split you just drag it from the app dock  you can even use the same app on both  sides of the screen which is useful for  transferring files in the files app and  it should work for third-party apps like  Microsoft Word but it doesn't seem to be  working yet in this first beta of iPad  OS within the Notes app you can even  grab a note and drag it to the side of  the screen to open both notes  side by side while the male app is open  you can compose a new email  and drag the composed view to the side  and either slide over or split view mode  hit cancel or sent and it'll  automatically close the coolest part is  that you can swipe along the bottom of  the screen to swipe between apps and all  the different split view app  combinations you previously had open  will be saved including as many versions  of each app as you'd like you can also  swipe with four fingers instead to  switch between apps or swipe up to get  to the home screen or swipe up and stop  at the center to open the app switcher  and choose the app you want to use if  you want to exit split view mode just  pull down on one of the apps tabs to get  into slide over mode then swipe it off  the screen now let's say you're at the  home screen and you want to start a  fresh version of an app but it keeps  opening up the same app that's already  in split view well simply tap and hold  on an app in the dock or on the home  screen and tap show all windows to open  the app expose from here you'll see the  various versions of the app currently  open and you can swipe to close them or  tap the plus icon to start fresh if you  want to get back to a different version  of the app you're currently using just  tap the same app within the app dock and  it'll open up that same app expose now  in Safari  we finally get automatic desktop mode  for browsing into split view just tap  and hold on a tab and drag it to the  edge of the screen you can also watch  videos in picture-in-picture mode if the  video player supports it by tapping the  pit button you can now swipe between  apps and use your iPad while the video  plays you can tap to pause closed or  bring it back to the Safari window you  can also drag it to any corner of the  screen and spread it with two fingers to  make the video larger you can use pip on  YouTube but it'll only play while the  tab is open and you can't move it around  but it's useful if you want to browse  YouTube Apple is also adding some text  editing features that can really speed  up your workflow you can quickly pick up  your cursor with one finger and move it  around anywhere you'd like or use two  fingers anywhere on the screen you can  also tap multiple times to select  different amounts of text tap twice to  select a word tap three times or for  some reason four times in this beta  version to select a sentence and tap  four times or for us five times to  select an entire paragraph you can then  pinch with three fingers to copy and  then spread with three fingers to paste  to undo you don't have to shake it  more just swipe left with three fingers  and then swipe right with three fingers  to redo and finally you can pinch with  two fingers on the keyboard to shrink it  and then grab the tab to move it  wherever you'd like on the screen  allowing you to type with just one thumb  or finger or use the new swype keyboard  feature then you can pinch with two  fingers again to bring it back to the  full keyboard so that was everything you  need to know about multitasking and  apple's new ipod OS if this video helped  you out make sure to tap that like  button and click the circle above to  subscribe thanks for watching and we'll  see you in the next video  [Music]
 

